KG42.register("rules-c89ece44ee3b7bbdd94a2568",{"id":"01-central_pool::v141-c-R007","paper":"01-central_pool","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The community microgrid operator redistributes revenues and costs among the members subject to the non-penalization condition. Scope: Redistribution of community revenues and costs among all member entities by the upper-level community operator. Condition: Each member's outcome within the community must be no worse than its outcome when acting individually. The entity-specific local market-clearing price is used to value the entity's energy exchanges with the community. Scope: Valuation of each entity's internal community energy exchanges at each time period in its energy revenues-and-costs account. Internal monetary flows offset one another except for the amount collected as the community operator's fee. Scope: Aggregate monetary flows for internal community energy exchanges. Condition: At the optimum of the lower level problem. Entities remain subject to the same external-grid electricity tariffs, fees and taxes as if they were outside the community. Scope: External-grid energy payments of entities belonging to the community. Condition: For energy exchanged with the external grid. The peak-power penalty is applied to the community's aggregate net energy flow with the grid. Scope: Community peak-power penalty remunerating the DSO for public-grid capacity. Condition: When entities aggregate in a community.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E002","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Aggregate monetary flows for internal community energy exchanges. | Community peak-power penalty remunerating the DSO for public-grid capacity. | External-grid energy payments of entities belonging to the community. | Redistribution of community revenues and costs among all member entities by the upper-level community operator. | Valuation of each entity's internal community energy exchanges at each time period in its energy revenues-and-costs account.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g04-E12"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"var_e_com_u_t","symbol":"e_{u,t}^{com}","meaning":"Energy exported to the community by entity u at time period t.","kind":"operational","domain":"R_+ (nonnegative real)","unit":"kWh","indices":["u ∈ U","t ∈ T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g01-e029","v141-b-g02-E16"]},{"variable_id":"var_i_com_u_t","symbol":"i_{u,t}^{com}","meaning":"Energy imported from the community by entity u at time period t.","kind":"operational","domain":"R_+ (nonnegative real)","unit":"kWh","indices":["u ∈ U","t ∈ T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g01-e029","v141-b-g02-E16"]},{"variable_id":"var_pi_com_u_t","symbol":"π_{u,t}^{com}","meaning":"Community market-clearing price for entity u at time period t, used to value internal community energy exchanges.","kind":"operational","domain":"R (real)","unit":"€/kWh","indices":["u ∈ U","t ∈ T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e025","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g04-E05"]},{"variable_id":"var_e_gri_u_t","symbol":"e_{u,t}^{gri}","meaning":"Energy exported to the external grid by entity u at time period t.","kind":"operational","domain":"R_+ (nonnegative real)","unit":"kWh","indices":["u ∈ U","t ∈ T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g01-e029"]},{"variable_id":"var_i_gri_u_t","symbol":"i_{u,t}^{gri}","meaning":"Energy imported from the external grid by entity u at time period t.","kind":"operational","domain":"R_+ (nonnegative real)","unit":"kWh","indices":["u ∈ U","t ∈ T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g01-e029"]},{"variable_id":"var_p_bar","symbol":"\\bar{p}","meaning":"Community peak power over the planning horizon, defined as the maximum net power imported from the grid by the community.","kind":"operational","domain":"R_+ (nonnegative real)","unit":"kW","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e024","v141-b-g02-E10"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"param_gamma_com","symbol":"γ^{com}","meaning":"Unitary fee of the community microgrid operator, collected on internal community energy exchanges.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e028","v141-b-g02-E15"]},{"parameter_id":"param_pi_peak","symbol":"π^{peak}","meaning":"Unitary cost (penalty) for peak power.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kW","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e016","v141-b-g01-e028","v141-b-g02-E10"]},{"parameter_id":"param_Delta_T","symbol":"Δ_T","meaning":"Duration of a time period.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"h","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e016","v141-b-g01-e028"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The community microgrid operator redistributes revenues and costs among the members subject to the non-penalization condition. Scope: Redistribution of community revenues and costs among all member entities by the upper-level community operator. Condition: Each member's outcome within the community must be no worse than its outcome when acting individually.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g02-E03"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The entity-specific local market-clearing price is used to value the entity's energy exchanges with the community. Scope: Valuation of each entity's internal community energy exchanges at each time period in its energy revenues-and-costs account.","expression":"- \\sum_{t\\in T} \\pi_{u,t}^{com} ( e_{u,t}^{com} - i_{u,t}^{com} )","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["var_pi_com_u_t","var_e_com_u_t","var_i_com_u_t"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g01-e025","v141-b-g04-E05"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Internal monetary flows offset one another except for the amount collected as the community operator's fee. Scope: Aggregate monetary flows for internal community energy exchanges. Condition: At the optimum of the lower level problem.","expression":"\\gamma^{com} \\sum_{u\\in U}\\sum_{t\\in T} ( e_{u,t}^{com} + i_{u,t}^{com} ) = - \\sum_{u\\in U}\\sum_{t\\in T} \\pi_{u,t}^{com} ( e_{u,t}^{com} - i_{u,t}^{com} )","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["var_e_com_u_t","var_i_com_u_t","var_pi_com_u_t"],"parameter_refs":["param_gamma_com"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g04-E12","v141-b-g03-e23","v141-b-g04-E13"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Entities remain subject to the same external-grid electricity tariffs, fees and taxes as if they were outside the community. Scope: External-grid energy payments of entities belonging to the community. Condition: For energy exchanged with the external grid.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g02-E29"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The peak-power penalty is applied to the community's aggregate net energy flow with the grid. Scope: Community peak-power penalty remunerating the DSO for public-grid capacity. Condition: When entities aggregate in a community.","expression":"\\bar{p} \\ge \\sum_{u\\in U} ( i_{u,t}^{gri} - e_{u,t}^{gri} ) / \\Delta_T \\quad \\forall t \\in T; \\quad \\text{peak-power penalty} = \\pi^{peak} \\bar{p}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["var_e_gri_u_t","var_i_gri_u_t","var_p_bar"],"parameter_refs":["param_Delta_T","param_pi_peak"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g01-e024","v141-b-g01-e016"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C006","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"For an entity exporting to the community and an entity importing from the community in the same time period, the buyer's community price equals the seller's community price plus twice the operator's unitary fee, because the fee is collected on both the import and the export.","expression":"\\pi_{u',t}^{com} = \\pi_{u,t}^{com} + 2\\gamma^{com} \\quad \\text{for } e_{u,t}^{com} > 0,\\ i_{u',t}^{com} > 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["var_pi_com_u_t"],"parameter_refs":["param_gamma_com"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E26","v141-b-g03-e01"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e001","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p01-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"T lettib, Antonio Giannitrapanib, Italy ext of community microgrids, where members of a community ca","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A market-oriented pricing of energy exchanges within the community is obtained by implementing an internal local market based on the marginal pricing scheme. The market aims at maximizing the social welfare of the community, thanks to the more efficient allocation of resources, the reduction of the peak power to be paid, and the increased amount of reserve, achieved at an aggregate level. A community microgrid operator, acting as a benevolent planner, redistributes revenues and costs among the members, in such a way that the solution achieved by each member within the community is not worse than the solution it would achieve by acting individually. In this way, each member is incentivized to participate in the community on a voluntary basis. The overall framework is formulated in the form of a bilevel model, where the lower level problem clears the market, while the upper level problem plays the role of the community microgrid operator."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. The community microgrid architecture","anchor_text":"community microgrids for the DSOs is that the coordinated optimiza- tion and control of several enti","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For the energy exchanged with the external grid, entities are subject to the same mechanism as if they would not be part of a community (electricity tariffs, fees, taxes, etc.). In practice, this requires a correction of the data communicated to operators and retailers for invoicing purposes. Indeed, assuming two meters per entity, the one will measure the energy flowing from the entity to the local bus, namely e^{gri}_u + e^{com}_u, the other will measure the energy flowing from the local bus to the entity, namely i^{gri}_u + i^{com}_u. Both measurements should be corrected with the information provided by the community microgrid operator (in particular, with the internal energy flows e^{com}_u and i^{com}_u) to obtain the correct values e^{gri}_u and i^{gri}_u to be invoiced to entity u."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1.2","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 242 (2019) 547–560 com (e ucom, t + i ucom, t ) = ucom, t ( eucom, t i ucom, t ). u t","equation_id":"(25)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"γ^com Σ_{u∈U} Σ_{t∈T} ( e_{u,t}^com + i_{u,t}^com ) = - Σ_{u∈U} Σ_{t∈T} π_{u,t}^com ( e_{u,t}^com - i_{u,t}^com ). (25) Intuitively, this can be explained because the monetary flows within the community offset each other, except for the part collected by the community operator, represented by its fee."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E16","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p06-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1.2","anchor_text":"ce u u u u ( ) nd be the total profit of entity u within the considered community mi- crogrid framew","equation_id":"(26)-(27)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"we let J_u = J_u^energy + J_u^reserve + J_u^peak (26) be the total profit of entity u within the considered community microgrid framework. In (26), the quantity J_u^energy takes into account the revenues and costs for entity u related to energy flows: J_u^energy = - Σ_{t∈T} ( Σ_{d∈D_u^she} π_{d,t}^she C_{d,t}^she Δ_τ a_{d,t}^she + Σ_{d∈D_u^ste} π_{d,t}^ste P_{d,t}^ste Δ_τ a_{d,t}^ste - π_t^egr e_{u,t}^gri + π_t^igr i_{u,t}^gri - π_{u,t}^com ( e_{u,t}^com - i_{u,t}^com ) + Σ_{d∈D_u^sto} γ_d^sto Δ_τ ( P̄_d η_d^cha a_{d,t}^cha + P̲_d/η_d^dis a_{d,t}^dis ) ). (27) Notice that the energy exchanges with the community, e_{u,t}^com and i_{u,t}^com, are valued at the price π_{u,t}^com, i.e., the market-clearing price for entity u at time t."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E30","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"3","anchor_text":"operationalplanning stage that optimizes day-ahead decisions with le time periods of T hours, given ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"It is stressed that, when entities aggregate in a community, the peak power penalty, which remunerates the DSO for the capacity of the public grid, is applied to the aggregate net energy flow Σ_{u∈U}(i_u^gri - e_u^gri). In this way, a single entity could see a decrease of its peak power costs, even if it does not lower its individual peak. However, adopting a peak penalty scheme of this type at the community level, would likely force the DSO to increase the peak penalty tariff. This, in turn, should incentivize community members to decrease and to desynchronize their peak power consumptions, which translates into lesser reinforcement costs for the DSO. Another positive impact of the community microgrids for the DSOs is that the coordinated optimization and control of several entities offer a simpler interface, e.g., for the procurement of flexibility services."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p13-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":13,"printed_page":"559","section":"Appendix C.1","anchor_text":"The strong duality condition requires the identity, at the optimum, of th function (B.1). Appendix C","equation_id":"(C.1),(C.2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-13.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"This appendix shows that identity (25) holds at the optimum of the lower level problem. First, we notice that\ne^{com}_{u,t} \\pi^{com}_{u,t} = e^{com}_{u,t} (\\mu_t - \\gamma^{com}).   (C.1)\nIf e^{com}_{u,t} = 0, the identity is trivial. If e^{com}_{u,t} > 0, it follows from the complementary slackness condition corresponding to the dual constraint (A.7), implying \\pi^{com}_{u,t} = \\mu_t - \\gamma^{com}. Similarly,\ni^{com}_{u,t} \\pi^{com}_{u,t} = i^{com}_{u,t} (\\mu_t + \\gamma^{com}),   (C.2)\nwhere the identity is trivial when i^{com}_{u,t} = 0, while it follows from the complementary slackness condition corresponding to the dual constraint (A.8), implying \\pi^{com}_{u,t} = \\mu_t + \\gamma^{com}, when i^{com}_{u,t} > 0."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. The community microgrid architecture","anchor_text":"operationalplanning stage that optimizes day-ahead decisions with le time periods of T hours, given ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"To achieve the aforementioned benefits, this paper focuses on the operational planning stage that optimizes day-ahead decisions with time periods of $\\Delta_T$ hours, given the grid energy prices, and the consumption and generation forecasts of the entities. An operator manages the community to maximize its social welfare, by optimizing the energy flows and the interactions among the entities and with the public grid. The operator must be contractually bound to the DSO, and its perimeter must be clearly defined. It must also be trusted by, and be contractually bound to, the community entities. The latter pay a fee to the operator for the remuneration of its activity."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e008","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. The community microgrid architecture","anchor_text":"operationalplanning stage that optimizes day-ahead decisions with le time periods of T hours, given ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"It is stressed that, when entities aggregate in a community, the peak power penalty, which remunerates the DSO for the capacity of the public grid, is applied to the aggregate net energy flow $\\sum_{u\\in\\mathcal{U}}(i^{gri}_u - e^{gri}_u)$. In this way, a single entity could see a decrease of its peak power costs, even if it does not lower its individual peak."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p05-c1r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1. The bilevel model","anchor_text":"B. Cornélusse, et al. the executed quantities, ad • the community prices, • the community symmetric ","equation_id":"(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Then, the role of the upper level is to share among the entities the profits of the community, by ensuring that no entity is penalized with respect to acting individually. Indeed, a community is composed of several entities driven by self-interests. In order to achieve a long-lasting community microgrid, each entity should be stimulated to participate in the community on a voluntary basis. This is achieved by enforcing the condition\n$J_u \\geq J_u^{SU} \\quad \\forall u \\in \\mathcal{U},$  (3)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e013","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1. The bilevel model","anchor_text":"y y y g g condition eu Ju JuSU u , (3) where JuSU is the optimal profit of entity u when acting indi","equation_id":"(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"where $J_u^{SU}$ is the optimal profit of entity u when acting individually, while $J_u$ is the profit of entity u within the community. As a consequence, the upper level can be seen as a benevolent planner, that manages the community microgrid in the best interest of all the participants. If at least one inequality in (3) is satisfied strictly, the state of the community is termed Pareto superior to the state when entities act individually [23]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e015","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1.1. Lower level problem","anchor_text":"y y y g g condition eu Ju JuSU u , (3) where JuSU is the optimal profit of entity u when acting indi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The vector y of decision variables is composed of the community symmetric reserve r^{sym}, the community peak power p̄, the executed quantities e^{gri}_{u,t}, i^{gri}_{u,t}, e^{com}_{u,t}, i^{com}_{u,t}, the community prices π^{com}_{u,t}, the upward and downward power reserves r^{s+}_{d,t}, r^{s-}_{d,t}, the fractions α^{she}_{d,t}, α^{ste}_{d,t} of shed demand and steered generation, the fractions of charging and discharging power α^{cha}_{d,t}, α^{dis}_{d,t} and the storage states of charge s_{d,t}. The objective function f is defined as follows:"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e016","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1.1. Lower level problem","anchor_text":"discharging power ad, t , ad , t , and the storage states of charge sdt, . The objective function f ","equation_id":"(4)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The objective function f is defined as follows:\n$-\\sum_{u\\in\\mathcal{U}}\\sum_{t\\in\\mathcal{T}}\\left(\\sum_{d\\in\\mathcal{D}_u^{she}} \\pi_{d,t}^{she} C_{d,t}^{she} \\alpha_{d,t}^{she} + \\sum_{d\\in\\mathcal{D}_u^{ste}} \\pi_{d,t}^{ste} P_{d,t}^{ste} \\Delta_T \\alpha_{d,t}^{ste} - \\pi_t^{egr} e_{u,t}^{gri} + \\pi_t^{igr} i_{u,t}^{gri} + \\gamma^{com}(e_{u,t}^{com} + i_{u,t}^{com}) + \\sum_{d\\in\\mathcal{D}_u^{sto}} \\gamma_d^{sto} \\Delta_T (\\bar{P}_d \\alpha_{d,t}^{cha} + \\underline{P}_d \\alpha_{d,t}^{dis}) \\right) + \\pi^{res} r^{sym} - \\pi^{peak} \\bar{p}.$  (4)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e020","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1.1. Lower level problem","anchor_text":"eugri, t i ugri, t + eucom, t i ucom, t nst ste ste3) T Pd, t + ad, t Pd, t u y, d unst d ste n- at ","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The second set of constraints is related to energy flows inside and outside the community.\n$e_{u,t}^{gri} - i_{u,t}^{gri} + e_{u,t}^{com} - i_{u,t}^{com} - \\Delta_T \\left( \\sum_{d \\in \\mathcal{D}_u^{nst}} P_{d,t}^{nst} + \\sum_{d \\in \\mathcal{D}_u^{ste}} \\alpha_{d,t}^{ste} P_{d,t}^{ste} \\right) + \\Delta_T \\left( \\sum_{d \\in \\mathcal{D}_u^{nfl}} C_{d,t}^{nfl} + \\sum_{d \\in \\mathcal{D}_u^{she}} \\left( 1 - \\alpha_{d,t}^{she} \\right) C_{d,t}^{she} \\right) + \\Delta_T \\sum_{d \\in \\mathcal{D}_u^{sto}} \\left( \\bar{P}_d \\alpha_{d,t}^{cha} - \\underline{P}_d \\alpha_{d,t}^{dis} \\right) = 0 \\quad \\forall u \\in \\mathcal{U}, \\forall t \\in \\mathcal{T} \\quad [\\pi_{u,t}^{com} \\in \\mathbb{R}]$  (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e024","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1.1. Lower level problem","anchor_text":"( i ugri, t e ugri, t )/ T p t . t peak 0 u (15) Constraint (11) defines the energy balance for each","equation_id":"(15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"$\\sum_{u \\in \\mathcal{U}} \\left( i_{u,t}^{gri} - e_{u,t}^{gri} \\right)/\\Delta_T \\leq \\bar{p} \\quad \\forall t \\in \\mathcal{T}. \\quad [\\varphi_t^{peak} \\geq 0]$  (15)\nFinally, constraint (15) determines the community peak power p̄. The community peak power p̄ is defined as the maximum of the net power imported from the grid by the community over the time horizon T. In this respect, the simultaneous import and export of different entities may have the effect of making the community peak power lower than the sum of the peaks of the entities when acting individually."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e025","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1.1. Lower level problem","anchor_text":"( i ugri, t e ugri, t )/ T p t . t peak 0 u (15) Constraint (11) defines the energy balance for each","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"It is stressed that the dual variable $\\pi_{u,t}^{com}$ of constraint (11) has an important economic interpretation within the marginal pricing framework [21,22]. Indeed, being $\\pi_{u,t}^{com}$ the dual variable of the energy balance constraint for entity u, in the proposed formulation it represents the market price at which entity u exchanges energy with the community at time t [33]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e028","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p02-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"Nomenclature","anchor_text":"d t,l p p p , s d she, kW rd Eucapt, maximum power export to the grid at time period t, with u , kW ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Parameters\n$C_{d,t}^{nfl}$ non-flexible power consumption at time period t, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{nfl}$, kW\n$C_{d,t}^{she}$ flexible power consumption at time period t, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{she}$, kW\n$E_{u,t}^{cap}$ maximum power export to the grid at time period t, with $u \\in \\mathcal{U}$, kW\n$I_{u,t}^{cap}$ maximum power import from the grid at time period t, with $u \\in \\mathcal{U}$, kW\n$P_{d,t}^{nst}$ non-steerable power generation at time period t, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{nst}$, kW\n$P_{d,t}^{ste}$ steerable power generation at time period t, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{ste}$, kW\n$\\bar{P}_d$ maximum charging power of battery d, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{sto}$, kW\n$\\underline{P}_d$ maximum discharging power of battery d, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{sto}$, kW\n$\\bar{S}_d$ maximum capacity of battery d, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{sto}$, kWh\n$\\underline{S}_d$ minimum capacity of battery d, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{sto}$, kWh\n$S_d^{init}$ initial state of charge of battery d, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{sto}$, kWh\n$S_d^{end}$ final state of charge of battery d, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{sto}$, kWh\n$J_u^{SU}$ optimal profit of entity u acting individually, €\n$\\gamma_d^{sto}$ unitary cost for usage of battery d, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{sto}$, €/kWh\n$\\gamma^{com}$ unitary fee of the community microgrid operator, €/kWh\n$\\eta_d^{cha}$ charging efficiency of battery d, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{sto}$\n$\\eta_d^{dis}$ discharging efficiency of battery d, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{sto}$\n$\\pi^{peak}$ unitary cost (penalty) for peak power, €/kW\n$\\pi^{res}$ unitary revenue for providing reserve capacity, €/kW\n$\\pi_{d,t}^{she}$ unitary cost of load shedding at time period t, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{she}$, €/kWh\n$\\pi_{d,t}^{ste}$ unitary cost of generating energy at time period t, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{ste}$, €/kWh\n$\\pi_t^{egr}$ unit price of energy exported to the grid at time period t, €/kWh\n$\\pi_t^{igr}$ unit price of energy imported from the grid at time period t, €/kWh\n$\\Delta_T$ duration of a time period, h"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e029","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p02-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"Nomenclature","anchor_text":"eucomt, + energy exported to the community at time period t by entity u , kWh eugrit, + energy expor","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Variables\n$\\alpha$ + slack variable to be maximized, €\n$\\alpha_{d,t}^{she}$ [0, 1] fraction of flexible power consumption that is shed at time period t, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{she}$\n$\\alpha_{d,t}^{ste}$ [0, 1] fraction of steerable power generation that is activated at time period t, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{ste}$\n$\\alpha_{d,t}^{cha}$ [0, 1] fraction of the maximum charging power used for battery d at time period t, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{sto}$\n$\\alpha_{d,t}^{dis}$ [0, 1] fraction of the maximum discharging power used for battery d at time period t, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{sto}$\n$e_{u,t}^{com}$ R_+ energy exported to the community at time period t by entity u, kWh\n$e_{u,t}^{gri}$ R_+ energy exported to the grid at time period t by entity u, kWh\n$i_{u,t}^{com}$ R_+ energy imported from the community at time period t by entity u, kWh\n$i_{u,t}^{gri}$ R_+ energy imported from the grid at time period t by entity u, kWh\n$\\bar{p}$ R_+ peak power of the microgrid over the planning horizon T, kW\n$\\bar{p}_u$ R_+ contribution to the peak power of the microgrid assigned to entity u, kW\n$r^{sym}$ R_+ symmetric power reserve provided by the microgrid through all periods of the planning horizon T, kW\n$r_u^{sym}$ R_+ contribution to the symmetric power reserve of the microgrid assigned to entity u, kW\n$r_{u,t}^{inc}$ R_+ upward reserve of power available at time period t and provided by entity u, kW\n$r_{u,t}^{dec}$ R_ downward reserve of power available at time period t and provided by entity u, kW\n$r_{d,t}^{s+}$ R_+ upward reserve of power available at time period t and provided by storage device d, kW\n$r_{d,t}^{s-}$ R_ downward reserve of power available at time period t and provided by storage device d, kW\n$s_{d,t}$ [S̲_d, S̄_d] state of charge of battery d at time period t, with $d \\in \\mathcal{D}^{sto}$, kWh\n$J_u$ R total profit of entity u acting in the community, €\n$J_u^{energy}$ R energy component of the profit of entity u, €\n$J_u^{peak}$ R_ peak power component of the profit of entity u, €\n$J_u^{reserve}$ R_ reserve component of the profit of entity u, €\n$J^*$ R optimal profit of the community microgrid, €\n\nDual Variables, and Corresponding Constraints\n$\\kappa_{d,t}^{s+}/\\kappa_{d,t}^{s-}$ R_+ storage upward/downward reserve, state of charge\n$\\mu_t$ R community energy balance\n$\\pi_{u,t}^{com}$ R entity energy balance\n$\\varphi_t^{inc}/\\varphi_t^{dec}$ R_+ symmetric reserve, upward/downward reserve\n$\\zeta_{d,t}$ R dynamics of battery state of charge\n$\\varphi_{d,t}^{she}/\\varphi_{d,t}^{ste}$ R_+ maximum load shedding/steerable generation\n$\\varphi_{d,t}^{cha}/\\varphi_{d,t}^{dis}$ R_+ maximum storage charging/discharging\n$\\varphi_{d,t}^{socUp}/\\varphi_{d,t}^{socLo}$ R_+ maximum/minimum battery state of charge\n$\\varphi_{u,t}^{eCap}/\\varphi_{u,t}^{iCap}$ R_+ maximum energy export/import to/from the grid\n$\\varphi_t^{peak}$ R_+ community peak power\n$\\varphi_{d,t}^{s+}/\\varphi_{d,t}^{s-}$ R_+ storage upward/downward reserve, power\n$\\xi_d$ R final battery state of charge"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p05-c1r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1","anchor_text":"B. Cornélusse, et al. the executed quantities, ad • the community prices, • the community symmetric ","equation_id":"(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to achieve a long-lasting community microgrid, each entity should be stimulated to participate in the community on a voluntary basis. This is achieved by enforcing the condition J_u >= J_u^SU, ∀u ∈ U, (3) where J_u^SU is the optimal profit of entity u when acting individually, while J_u is the profit of entity u within the community. As a consequence, the upper level can be seen as a benevolent planner, that manages the community microgrid in the best interest of all the participants. If at least one inequality in (3) is satisfied strictly, the state of the community is termed Pareto superior to the state when entities act individually [23]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1.1","anchor_text":"eugri, t i ugri, t + eucom, t i ucom, t nst ste ste3) T Pd, t + ad, t Pd, t u y, d unst d ste n- at ","equation_id":"(15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Σ_{u∈U} ( i_{u,t}^gri - e_{u,t}^gri )/Δ_τ \u003c= p̄, ∀t ∈ T. [φ_t^peak >= 0] (15) Finally, constraint (15) determines the community peak power p̄. The community peak power p̄ is defined as the maximum of the net power imported from the grid by the community over the time horizon T. In this respect, the simultaneous import and export of different entities may have the effect of making the community peak power lower than the sum of the peaks of the entities when acting individually."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.1.1","anchor_text":"com com 1 1,1 = 0.055 €/kWh, which includes the market price 2,1 of entity 2, and the fee com due to","equation_id":"(37)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"This reflects the following relation, which is derived from (C.1) and (C.2) for an entity u with e_{u,t}^com > 0, and an entity u′ with i_{u′,t}^com > 0: π_{u,t}^com = π_{u′,t}^com + 2γ^com. (37)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E29","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"3","anchor_text":"community microgrids for the DSOs is that the coordinated optimiza- tion and control of several enti","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For the energy exchanged with the external grid, entities are subject to the same mechanism as if they would not be part of a community (electricity tariffs, fees, taxes, etc.). In practice, this requires a correction of the data communicated to operators and retailers for invoicing purposes. Indeed, assuming two meters per entity, the one will measure the energy flowing from the entity to the local bus, namely e_u^gri + e_u^com, the other will measure the energy flowing from the local bus to the entity, namely i_u^gri + i_u^com. Both measurements should be corrected with the information provided by the community microgrid operator (in particular, with the internal energy flows e_u^com and i_u^com) to obtain the correct values e_u^gri and i_u^gri to be invoiced to entity u."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e01","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":"554","section":"4.1.1","anchor_text":"com com 1 1,1 = 0.055 €/kWh, which includes the market price 2,1 of entity 2, and the fee com due to","equation_id":"(37)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"This reflects the following relation, which is derived from (C.1) and (C.2) for an entity u with e_{u,t}^{com} > 0, and an entity u' with i_{u',t}^{com} > 0:\n\n\\pi_{u',t}^{com} = \\pi_{u,t}^{com} + 2\\gamma^{com}.   (37)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p12-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"558","section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"s + dis s socUp socLo d , T d , T + d, T + d d , T d + chad, T = 0 T d T The dual constraints of euc","equation_id":"(A.7), (A.8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The dual constraints of e_{u,t}^{com} >= 0 and i_{u,t}^{com} >= 0 are respectively:\n\n\\pi_{u,t}^{com} - \\mu_t \\geq -\\gamma^{com}   (A.7)\n\n-\\pi_{u,t}^{com} + \\mu_t \\geq -\\gamma^{com}   (A.8)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p12-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"558","section":"Appendix A. Lower level dual constraints","anchor_text":"(A.6) (A.7) (A.8) (A.9) (A.10) (A.11) (A.12) (A.13)","equation_id":"(A.7),(A.8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The dual constraints of e^{com}_{u,t} \\ge 0 and i^{com}_{u,t} \\ge 0 are respectively\n\\pi^{com}_{u,t} - \\mu_t \\ge -\\gamma^{com}   (A.7)\n-\\pi^{com}_{u,t} + \\mu_t \\ge -\\gamma^{com}   (A.8)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p13-c1r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":13,"printed_page":"559","section":"Appendix C.1","anchor_text":"= eu , t µ t com i u , t µt + com t u t u = µt eucom, t i ucom, t com e ucom, t + i ucom, t t u u t ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-13.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"By using (C.1) and (C.2), we obtain:\n\\sum_{t \\in T} \\sum_{u \\in U} \\pi^{com}_{u,t} (e^{com}_{u,t} - i^{com}_{u,t}) = \\sum_{t \\in T} \\sum_{u \\in U} e^{com}_{u,t} (\\mu_t - \\gamma^{com}) - \\sum_{t \\in T} \\sum_{u \\in U} i^{com}_{u,t} (\\mu_t + \\gamma^{com}) = \\sum_{t \\in T} \\sum_{u \\in U} \\mu_t (e^{com}_{u,t} - i^{com}_{u,t}) - \\gamma^{com} \\sum_{u} \\sum_{t} (e^{com}_{u,t} + i^{com}_{u,t}) = -\\gamma^{com} \\sum_{t \\in T} \\sum_{u \\in U} (e^{com}_{u,t} + i^{com}_{u,t}),\nwhere the last equality holds due to (12)."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e001","quote":"A community microgrid operator, acting as a benevolent planner, redistributes revenues and costs among the members, in such a way that the solution achieved by each member within the community is not worse than the solution it would achieve by acting individually."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E16","quote":"Notice that the energy exchanges with the community, e_{u,t}^com and i_{u,t}^com, are valued at the price π_{u,t}^com, i.e., the market-clearing price for entity u at time t."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15","quote":"Intuitively, this can be explained because the monetary flows within the community offset each other, except for the part collected by the community operator, represented by its fee."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E12","quote":"This appendix shows that identity (25) holds at the optimum of the lower level problem."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","quote":"For the energy exchanged with the external grid, entities are subject to the same mechanism as if they would not be part of a community (electricity tariffs, fees, taxes, etc.)."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E30","quote":"It is stressed that, when entities aggregate in a community, the peak power penalty, which remunerates the DSO for the capacity of the public grid, is applied to the aggregate net energy flow Σ_{u∈U}(i_u^gri - e_u^gri)."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"a5c013608d765f268e68ec84607a04c226900a9cb7450a635f5e5c9b0407a65b","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The rule has source-supported mathematical expressions for the settlement-payment identity (25), the valuation of internal community exchanges at π_{u,t}^{com} in J_u^{energy} (27), the peak-penalty aggregate-flow basis (15), and the buyer-seller fee-spread relation (37). Non-penalization (C001) and external-grid invoicing correction (C004) remain procedural/not formalized because their full mathematical objects (derived profits and tariff formulas) are not present in this rule's frozen graph and supplied evidence.","bindings":[{"object_id":"var_e_com_u_t","node_ids":["settlement.payment","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E002"],"rationale":"e_{u,t}^{com} is an internal community energy export valued at the local clearing price π_{u,t}^{com} and settled in the entity account; the pricing.local→settlement.payment edge records this valuation link."},{"object_id":"var_i_com_u_t","node_ids":["settlement.payment","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E002"],"rationale":"i_{u,t}^{com} is an internal community energy import valued at the local clearing price π_{u,t}^{com} and settled in the entity account; the pricing.local→settlement.payment edge records this valuation link."},{"object_id":"var_pi_com_u_t","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E002"],"rationale":"π_{u,t}^{com} is the local market-clearing price for entity u at time t, produced under pricing.local and used by settlement.payment to value community exchanges."},{"object_id":"var_e_gri_u_t","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"External-grid energy export enters the entity's external-grid payment/settlement account and is outside the internal community pricing edge."},{"object_id":"var_i_gri_u_t","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"External-grid energy import enters the entity's external-grid payment/settlement account and is outside the internal community pricing edge."},{"object_id":"var_p_bar","node_ids":["settlement.payment","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"Community peak power determines the peak-power penalty that the community operator passes to settlement; the operator→settlement edge links this settlement responsibility."},{"object_id":"param_gamma_com","node_ids":["settlement.payment","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"γ^{com} is the unitary operator fee collected on internal community exchanges and distributed through settlement; the operator→settlement edge records the operator's fee role."},{"object_id":"param_pi_peak","node_ids":["settlement.payment","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"π^{peak} is the unitary peak-power penalty applied to the community peak and settled by the operator."},{"object_id":"param_Delta_T","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Δ_T is the time-period duration needed to convert settled energy quantities to peak power in the peak-penalty expression."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"The non-penalization/redistribution condition is enforced by the community operator and affects the settlement/payment outcome; E001 is the operator→settlement link."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E002"],"rationale":"The entity-specific local price is used to value community exchanges in the entity's revenue-and-cost account; E002 is the pricing→settlement link."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","node_ids":["settlement.payment","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"Identity (25) states internal monetary flows offset except the operator fee; E001 records the operator fee's settlement relation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C004","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"External-grid tariffs, fees and taxes remain applicable to community entities; this is a settlement.payment procedure."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C005","node_ids":["settlement.payment","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"The peak-power penalty is applied to the community aggregate net grid flow and remunerates the DSO; the operator→settlement edge captures the community-level settlement."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C006","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E002"],"rationale":"The buyer-seller community price relation with 2γ^{com} is a settlement/payment consequence of local pricing; E002 links pricing.local to settlement.payment."}],"revision_requests":["C001: The non-penalization condition J_u ≥ J_u^{SU} (and its generalized form J_u ≥ J_u^{SU} + α, α ≥ 0) is source-supported but not formalized here because J_u is a derived entity profit and J_u^{SU} is a stand-alone optimal-profit parameter not included in this rule's declared x/theta; C.1 should add typed objects (and any participation node) if this condition is to be represented inside v141-c-R007.","C004: The external-grid invoicing correction (metered e_{u,t}^{gri}+e_{u,t}^{com} and i_{u,t}^{gri}+i_{u,t}^{com} corrected by internal flows) and the 'same tariffs, fees, taxes' condition lack an explicit tariff/fee formula in the supplied evidence; B re-extraction of the exact invoicing equations is required before formalization.","C005: Individual peak-cost allocation J_u^{peak} = −π^{peak} \\bar{p}_u and the sharing identities r^{sym}=Σ_u r_u^{sym}, \\bar{p}=Σ_u \\bar{p}_u, and Σ_u J_u=J* are not represented in this rule's V/E; if they belong to settlement, C.1 should add the corresponding coordination/settlement objects or confirm they belong to v141-c-R003.","B transcription uncertainties remain for equations (A.3)-(A.6) and (B.1) (sign/placement of storage-bound dual terms and summation sets); these do not affect the expressions formalized here, but should be resolved before other rules rely on them."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
